# v38: Target-direct MICRO planner is PRIMARY: Target Model owns semantic location; bounded local ACTIVE/HOLD + existing hard mechanics own execution geometry.
# v38: Existing v37 E156 crease/role planner remains intact as FALLBACK only when Target-direct is physically/safety blocked.
# v38: Target correction, frozen binding/executor, Action hard-negative separation, and model-only automatic FINISH remain unchanged from v37.
# v40: preserves v39 and adds bounded ACTIVE+HOLD+actual-PULL recovery only after normal + v39 recovery failure, plus split NO_PLAN failure diagnostics.
# v40: no reach/path/pair/board/contact-Z safety relaxation; exact PULL trials are capped and ACTIVE-diversified to avoid exhaustive-search latency.
# v39: preserves v38 Target-direct primary + E156 fallback and adds bounded reach-aware HOLD recovery only after normal HOLD/pair failure.
# v39: no reach/path/pair/board/contact-Z safety relaxation; FINISH model-only and Target/hard-negative semantics remain unchanged.
# v42: v41 baseline + AUTO FULL-E156 default OFF, cached/deduplicated Target-direct failure work, and final BACKOFF reconciliation of provisional PEEL uncertainty.
# v43: production AUTO defaults disable VLA/MICRO human collection-review gates while preserving debug/shadow logs and every physical safety/binding check.
# v43: LONG_PULL full prefreeze is lazy in production AUTO: keep immediate full planning only when AUTO-X decision arbitration requires it, otherwise defer exact resolved motion until LONG_PULL remains the final executable action after model routing.
# v44: reliable 8..14deg Pose-angle confirmation is lazy: defer expensive ROTATE pair-plan construction until fresh angle consensus PASS; >14deg remains immediate.
# upper_runtime_v51: modular integration adapter added to final standalone v51 without changing v51 Action/BMR/Target/planner/motion policy. Standalone execution remains available; imported controller mode is headless and uses the main-owned camera.
# v47: bounded MICRO rescue admission is quick_gate OR already-computed same-X strong structural/CCA fold evidence; Target>=threshold + light planner READY + unchanged hard safety remain mandatory.
# v47: FINISH may be vetoed only by a stricter strong-CCA fold guard followed by Target+planner+safety confirmation; legacy FINISH heuristics still cannot terminate AUTO-X.
# v47: no garment photometric normalization and no extra camera/Seg/Pose/wrinkle inference are added; inputs remain byte-path compatible with v44/v46.
# v48: Target-direct validates the learned Target against already-computed same-X READY-CCA fold geometry; wrong-component Targets are fail-closed before FAST/FULL fallback.
# v48: Target-direct pull direction is locked to the validated crease normal (centroid-away BODY->flap sign), reuses E122 same-fold ACTIVE/HOLD role validation, and bounds E111 contour-normal drift.
# v48: no new camera/Seg/Pose/wrinkle inference; validation uses only cached READY-CCA board-mm component summaries and adds explicit target/direction latency diagnostics.
# v51: preserves v49 Action/BMR/top-K Target/local-fold selection and CENTER guard; after Target validation the complete MICRO planner geometry is restored to v44 behavior in matching core_v51.
# v51: ACTIVE/HOLD, pull_hint, outer-normal direction, pull distance, endpoint and bounded reach/recovery are v44-carried; executor/contact-Z and every hard safety threshold remain unchanged.
# v49: replaces v48 CCA hard authority with top-K Target peaks + same-X cached local wrinkle/crease validation; READY-CCA is soft support only.
# v49: selected local crease context supplies bounded direction/role validation; no extra TensorRT/YOLO/Pose/UniDepth/full-frame wrinkle inference is added.
# v49: CENTER routing guard preserves AUTO-X strong NORMAL LONG_PULL below the 90mm gross-center band and preserves light circumcenter nudge variants instead of promoting them to full CENTER.
# v41: v40 baseline + PULL-direction reach recovery/FAST target-local planner ordering in core + MICRO live pull/peel timing optimization.
# v37: preserves v36 MICRO action/Target review separation and same-X corrected-Target E156 replanning before motion.
# v37: FINISH authority is model-only in automatic mode: legacy A109/CCA/rotation-ready logic stays diagnostic/planner context but cannot terminate AUTO-X by itself.
# v37: Target corrections remain separate from Action hard-negatives and now persist fallback snapshot assets when no decision-debug bundle is available.
#!/usr/bin/env python3
# v35: v32 planner/motion preserved; hard-negative collection is fail-closed on NOT_MICRO from both READY-MICRO review and MICRO-plan-failure annotation.
# v35: NONE/NOT_MICRO is now a control intercept, not a passive annotation: current MICRO/fallback auto-execution is latched off until a corrected macro is selected, manually ENTERed, and reviewed GOOD/BAD/SKIP.
# v35: Action NOT_MICRO remains completely separate from Target-Model NONE; no Target NONE label is written by this path.
# v32: after the complete v31 path fails, retry flipped normal/role on a small number of real creases, then run one target-local recovery from already-computed RGB crease maps.
# v32: no new full-frame perception, no safety-threshold relaxation, and per-stage primary/flipped/target-local latency is logged.
# v31 FINAL STANDALONE: v30 target-guided planner preserved; E156 pair search optimized without safety/threshold relaxation.
# v31: v29 ranked fallback, human annotation, debug capture, and v26 fixed-contact-Z execution remain unchanged.
# v31: MICRO failure annotation and AUTO-X diagnostic bundles remain unchanged from v29.
# v26 FINAL STANDALONE: v25 full-auto/model integration + fixed-Z MICRO ACTIVE contact execution.
# v26: ACTIVE_CONTACT_FLOOR keeps the existing planner/clamped fixed contact Z command but no longer waits for a symmetric T:105 exact-Z arrival gate; it uses the same descent-settle timing style as CENTER before pull verification.
# v26: contact-floor safety clamp, frozen XY/arm assignment, pull XY-effect + Z-lock verification, peel/clear checks, and verified standby recovery remain unchanged.
# v25 FINAL STANDALONE: v24 physical/planner baseline + top_board_state_micro_v2 hybrid action model + micro_target_v2 target selector.
# v25: one X arms a full-auto judge -> execute -> standby -> fresh rejudge loop through FINISH; ordinary ENTER approval is no longer required in standalone_full_auto mode.
# v25: VLA/MICRO/CCA dataset persistence stays in the code but defaults OFF; runtime inference is independently controlled by vla_runtime_enable.
# v25: learned MICRO target selects only among already-safe E156 crease candidates; no heuristic target fallback is allowed when TARGET/NONE or target-to-safe-crease binding fails.
# v25: repeated MICRO target/plan unavailability triggers a fresh rejudge and suppresses model MICRO once after two consecutive failures, preventing an endless MICRO/NONE loop.
# vla_0856_micro_unfold_v18: v17 baseline + frozen-observation label/action lock and same-observation data binding.
# v19: MICRO_PLAN_BAD records correct MICRO action + wrong rule plan without executing it; action-model supervision stays MICRO_UNFOLD.
# v19: CENTER selection freezes the exact ordinary CENTER plan, previews it, and Enter reuses that same plan with zero geometry rebuild.
# v19: frozen TARGET point remains saved but is hidden from the live UI while robot motion is active.
# v20: load the co-located MICRO core by the main file's version suffix, eliminating stale hard-coded core-module imports.
# v20: correctly executed + human-GOOD MICRO_UNFOLD transitions follow the normal VLA training-eligibility rule; the old global MICRO quarantine is removed.
# v23: MICRO executor clamps only the physical ACTIVE contact/pull Z to a reachable floor (default -89mm) while preserving the frozen planner floor for audit; dedicated contact-arrival tolerance defaults to 6mm.
# v23: ROTATE post-grip failure recovery initializes its vertical retract speed locally before every recovery path, eliminating the vertical_retract_spd NameError without changing the normal rotation trajectory.
# v24: MICRO post-action return latency optimization only. Imaging-standby physical arrival remains fail-closed and sequential, but default timeout is 4.0s, XY/Z tolerances are 35/30mm, and one valid T:105 sample is sufficient.
# v24: _wait_clear_or_soft keeps the same measured safe-clear Z/XY invariants and vertical-clear commands, while default timeout is 2.5s, per-feedback wait is 0.35s, and polling interval is 0.05s.
# v22: MICRO action-model label locking is enforced per observation.  If PLAN_BAD/NO_PLAN locks MICRO_UNFOLD as the supervision label, a later physical fallback action from that exact observation is preserved for audit but forced training_eligible=False.
# v22: ABORT/FAILED is blocked while MICRO_UNFOLD is selected with no executable frozen plan unless PLAN_BAD/NO_PLAN supervision has first been saved (or the operator changes/rejudges the action).
# v21: MICRO_NO_PLAN records that MICRO_UNFOLD is the correct macro but no executable frozen MICRO plan exists; no robot motion is sent.
# v21: MICRO_NO_PLAN and MICRO_PLAN_BAD both preserve explicit action-model supervision in the exact same-observation decision/target record, while planner outcome is stored separately.
# - Every persisted frozen VLA observation gets one explicit target-model label before the workflow may advance: camera LEFT CLICK=TARGET; VLA panel buttons=NONE/CANCEL/UNKNOWN-SKIP.
# - The target label UI is action-agnostic: CENTER/SPREAD/ORTHO/LONG_PULL/MICRO/ROTATE/FINISH/REJUDGE scenes all contribute target-model data.
# - Missing input is never interpreted as NONE. New X/automatic rejudge/physical approval/REJUDGE are fail-closed while the current observation remains UNLABELED.
# - v18: a saved observation is annotation-locked until TARGET/NONE/UNKNOWN is explicit; action buttons are disabled before that label.
# - v18: non-executable planner REJUDGE results become a same-snapshot HUMAN_REJUDGE hold in VLA collection, preserving all frozen alternatives for human action selection instead of silently advancing.
# - v18: target-sample/decision binding is observation-id exact; a new sample can never overwrite the previous observation's decision JSON.
# - v18: camera TARGET clicks are accepted only while the exact current frozen observation is UNLABELED and robot/inference are idle; relabel requires CANCEL/RELABEL first.
# - v18: frozen WAIT_ENTER target invalidation ignores brightness-only pixel drift and uses foreground shape change; UNLABELED annotation frames never auto-invalidate.
# - Target-model records reference the authoritative observation JSON + all persisted camera/board/mask/heatmap files and preserve current action/model/planner context; collection stays separate from VLA classifier training.
# - SPREAD no longer trusts the former fixed ~0.18s close settle alone. T:105 gripper t must show sufficient close progress and consecutive stability on BOTH arms before LIFT/SPREAD.
# - A failed SPREAD gripper barrier suppresses lift/stretch and performs OPEN -> same-XY hover retract; no pull is authorized from an unconfirmed grip.
# - V14 MICRO planner/executor, sequential-air collision mitigation, hard safety and uncertain-result handling remain unchanged.
# - V14 MICRO approach/return forbids simultaneous large dual-arm XY travel: each arm rises/moves/descends sequentially, and standby return is physically verified one arm at a time.
# - A verified XY pull followed by peel/backoff Z under-run is EXECUTED_BUT_UNCERTAIN, not AUTO-X FAILED; cleanup completes safely and a fresh automatic rejudge follows.
# - True pull/feedback/safety/standby failures remain hard FAILED and keep the existing fail-closed recovery policy.
# - The stale args.press_board_margin reference now uses the existing targeted_press_board_margin setting; no new margin threshold is introduced.
# - V13 never drops an already complete safe MICRO plan merely because later alternate-candidate search fails.
# - Same-crease recovery may move ACTIVE/HOLD anchors only along the exact detected crease; all hard reach/board/path/pair safety remains unchanged.
# - MICRO target-fold labels are stored separately from the VLA training set; camera left-click labels TARGET and VLA-panel buttons handle NONE/CANCEL/UNKNOWN-SKIP.
# - Target-fold clicks are DATA LABELS ONLY in V13 and never modify the frozen robot plan.
# - V11 never reintroduces a global "garment sufficiently spread" gate; MICRO remains local fold/crease + hard-safety driven.
# - Near-contour branches may survive only with garment-relative RGB step, Pose deformation support, low seam overlap and real STRUCTURAL evidence.
# - If one RGB crease cannot produce a safe pair, other real same-snapshot execution creases are ranked and tried before blocking.
# - The exact plan-generating crease is kept only locally through final role validation, then omitted from the frozen execution plan.
# - CENTER/SPREAD/pose-symmetry/finish readiness are diagnostic only for MICRO; they no longer block plan generation.
# - Macro garment-state selection remains the responsibility of the Board+State model/AUTO-X layer.
# - MICRO admission is local: Pose/RGB fold evidence + exact same-crease ACTIVE/HOLD geometry + hard mechanical safety.
# - RGB rescue remains garment-relative; no absolute garment-brightness or new center-error threshold is introduced.
# - If base geometry fails 420mm reach, V10 first keeps V9 HOLD-only tangent recovery, then may move BOTH ACTIVE/HOLD along the SAME crease tangent.
# - Pair spacing 66..126mm, 65mm path clearance, 420mm hard reach, board bounds and both-arm assignment checks are unchanged.
# - Final role validation now uses the exact crease/region that generated the plan before falling back to joint-state masks.
# - MICRO plan geometry remains unchanged; V20 removes only the VLA training quarantine.
# - MICRO location is no longer chosen by Pose intrusion alone: Pose/deformation proposes a ROI and a same-ROI E122 RGB EXECUTION Fold-Crease must corroborate the real boundary.
# - Pure NECK evidence, uncorroborated Pose regions, group=NONE, and unrelated generic FOLD_NORMAL/EDGE fallbacks cannot publish a READY MICRO plan in strict mode.
# - When strong TORSO_QUAD/CHAIN deformation exists, inconsistent raw intrusion groups cannot steal location authority.
# - V14 preserves V13 contact/pull geometry but changes air-travel sequencing and uncertain peel classification.
# - ACTIVE now stages from active_start_z to the frozen active_floor_z before pulling; the main pull is Z-locked at that lower interaction Z.
# - PEEL verification uses a 35mm default measured-clearance threshold (dynamic floor 30mm) instead of the over-strict fixed 42mm criterion that caused repeat false FAILs.
# - PEEL and vertical CLEAR soft-pass conditions are evaluated on every T:105 poll and return immediately once physically satisfied; they no longer wait for exact-target timeout first.
# - Restores the missing _press_board_points_from_plan helper used by ACTION3/LONG_PULL passive-hold snapping, eliminating repeated NameError fallbacks.
# - Pull verification now uses measured XY progress + a 7mm Z-lock tolerance instead of a brittle 3mm-only hard failure.
# - Peel/HOLD clear accept measured safe clearance when the exact high-Z target saturates; failed actions still remain failed.
# - Error cleanup is FULL OPEN -> measured same-XY safe clear -> physically VERIFIED camera-clear standby. MICRO outer A140 audit now distinguishes a sent standby command from verified arrival, so a failed standby cannot silently suppress the physical-recovery latch.
# - E128 no-depth fast path removes zero-UniDepth percentile work; same-X caches + bounded crease anchors reduce plan_points latency while preserving hard board/420mm reach/65mm path safety.
# - Frozen MICRO plans are now compact execution-only dictionaries; 720p masks/maps/branch diagnostics never enter pending_auto_x_action, preventing control-panel deepcopy stalls.
# - E130 directional pair search reuses cached ray geometry and exact candidate transforms; repeated full-frame morphology/Homography inversion per ACTIVE x HOLD pair is removed without relaxing board/reach/path safety.
# - MICRO quick gate rejects weak single-neck/contour-only hints unless supported by stronger deformation/structural evidence, preventing ~50s heavy planning on nearly-flat shirts.
# - Structured MICRO stage timing is logged for gate/RGB/geometry/branch/directional/finalize so future regressions are visible.
# - MICRO_UNFOLD is a regular VLA semantic action for data collection, but Board+State model/AUTO-X never selects it automatically in this release.
# - One lightweight same-snapshot gate reuses the existing authoritative garment mask + cached T-shirt Pose + existing structural hint; only suspicious cases run the heavy E156 RGB Fold-Crease planner.
# - E156 camera, segmentation, Pose inference, independent I->X UI, and UniDepth runtime are NOT imported. The exact current VLA X RGB/mask/Pose/H/config are reused.
# - A safe E156 HOLD/ACTIVE/pull plan is precomputed before CENTER/ROTATE/FINISH priority returns and frozen with a deterministic binding id. Human MICRO_UNFOLD can execute only that exact X-frozen plan; no Enter-time replan is allowed.
# - NORMAL LONG_PULL is also precomputed before early priority returns. Both AUTO-X normal LONG_PULL and human LONG_PULL bind the exact same-X preview + resolved motion plan with a deterministic id; no Enter-time rebuild is allowed.
# - E156 fold-crease/pose-deformation/contour/EDGE-cluster/exact-normal geometry and hard board/reach/path safety remain unchanged in micro_unfold_e156_core_v23.py (byte-identical carry-forward from v22).
# - V12 does not add a new detector or macro-state gate: all already-retained crease candidates are completed through existing mechanics + exact-role validation, then the best READY plan is selected.
# - Human MICRO_UNFOLD selection draws only the frozen selected plan (crease, ACTIVE, HOLD, pull direction, arms) on the existing camera view; no extra candidate panel/window is added.
# - Physical MICRO_UNFOLD preserves HOLD + CLOSED ACTIVE Z-locked pull + diagonal peel + E152 12mm tension backoff; V14 explicitly vertically clears BOTH arms before full-open and sequential standby/rejudge.
# vla_0854_hybrid_model_autox_fp32: vla_0852_stage3 + Board+State v2 TensorRT FP32 HYBRID DECISION.
# - AUTO-X Stage3 still runs first on the same snapshot and freezes its existing safe alternate plans.
# - Model may select only CENTER/SPREAD/ROTATE/FINISH after confidence+margin gates; LONG_PULL/ORTHO/PRESS stay AUTO-X fallback-only.
# - Model selection binds only already-frozen Stage3 plans; missing/unsafe binding restores the original AUTO-X pending action fail-closed.
# - Dedicated model binder avoids the human UI motion/yolo busy guard inside the X worker; final Enter safety stays unchanged.
# - Hybrid mode requires ENTER/SPACE for every physical action; no model path directly dispatches robot motion.
# - Historical model PRESS class remains audit-only and never restores physical PRESS.
# vla_0852_stage3: stage2 baseline + standalone/manual/automatic PRESS execution routes retired; LONG_PULL targeted_press primitives preserved. No Shadow or MICRO_UNFOLD.
# - VLA PNG/JSON persistence is removed from vla_dataset_lock and observation bundles use a bounded background writer queue.
# - VLA control-panel state reads are non-blocking and reuse the last cached snapshot while shared state is briefly busy.
# - READY pose symmetry reuses the same-snapshot cached Pose keypoints + authoritative garment mask; duplicate Pose/Seg inference is disabled.
# - Seg/Pose TensorRT wrappers and run metadata are preloaded before the first X judgment.
# - Separate latency logs cover ROTATE pair planning, pose symmetry, VLA enqueue, and background persistence I/O.
# - Queue saturation falls back to synchronous save OUTSIDE the dataset lock; shutdown flushes queued observations.
# vla_0852_stage1: clean pre-MICRO_UNFOLD baseline derived directly from vla_0852.
# - Retire the standalone VLA/AUTO-X PRESS (legacy ACTION4) macro: no planner selection, no VLA button/override, and no physical dispatcher branch.
# - Preserve LONG_PULL/ACTION3 targeted-press primitives and motion helpers because LONG_PULL still depends on them.
# - Stage3 removes W/manual lane smoothing and coarse-X auto lane/targeted PRESS execution; only LONG_PULL/ACTION3 targeted_press execution remains.
