# - CENTER/SPREAD/ORTHO_SPREAD/LONG_PULL/ROTATE/FINISH/REJUDGE behavior is otherwise kept from vla_0852.
# vla_0852: remove legacy fold-diagnostic visual overlay (cyan R-lines / red confirmed ridge); diagnostic computation/logging/data are preserved.
# vla_0851 behavior is otherwise preserved: moderate CENTER-vs-LONG_PULL recommendation competition and no POST_FINISH motion.
# - CENTER error >=90mm keeps the existing hard CENTER priority with no LONG_PULL competition.
# - In the existing CENTER trigger band (default 50..90mm), evaluate one same-snapshot ordinary ACTION3/LONG_PULL preview and motion plan before returning CENTER.
# - Only an existing canonical strong LONG_PULL (same >=80mm length / >=2.7 aspect thresholds, non-structural, non-repeat, executable motion plan) may override CENTER as the AUTO-X recommendation.
# - A weaker but safe ordinary LONG_PULL preview remains frozen for VLA human override while AUTO-X still recommends CENTER. No LONG_PULL thresholds, geometry, pull distance, robot safety, inference, or human selection authority are changed.
# vla_0850: FOLD diagnostic fast gate; POST_FINISH remains disabled.
# - Preserve vla_0849 FOLD_SUSPECT/FOLD_RIDGE/FOLD_CONFIRMED thresholds and geometry, but evaluate the expensive multi-threshold heatmap ridge path ONLY when same-snapshot Pose evidence is already FOLD_SUSPECT.
# - If Pose is normal/unavailable, ridge connected-components/PCA clustering is skipped entirely and an explicit POSE_GATE_SKIP status is cached/logged for that inference serial.
# - Add lightweight per-stage timing (pose_ms/ridge_ms/total_ms) so Jetson logs can verify the optimization without adding inference or planner work.
# - No extra snapshot, YOLO, Pose, heatmap, CCA, candidate search, PRESS action, or robot motion is introduced. LONG_PULL diagnostics and FINISH-no-POST_FINISH policy remain unchanged.
# vla_0849: diagnostic-only Pose + multi-threshold heatmap fold detection; POST_FINISH motion removed.
# - HUMAN FINISH now ends with terminal VLA save/episode close only. The historical POST_FINISH_TOP_ALIGN planner/executor remains dead reference code but is not frozen, advertised, or executed from any FINISH path.
# - Add diagnostic-only FOLD_SUSPECT from semantic Pose keypoints that sit abnormally deep inside the current real garment mask. Use region evidence (LEFT/RIGHT_SLEEVE, NECK, HEM), not a single keypoint, and use a separate deeper allowance for naturally concave armpit landmarks.
# - Add diagnostic-only FOLD_RIDGE from the existing wrinkle heatmap using multiple relative intensity percentiles, so a long connected ridge may be detected even when it is not a bright/red wrinkle response. No extra camera snapshot, YOLO, Pose, or heatmap inference is introduced.
# - FOLD_CONFIRMED requires BOTH a Pose semantic-region suspect and a long heatmap ridge geometrically near that region. Results are logged, drawn on the overlay, and persisted in observation state_summary only; PRESS/AUTO-X action choice and physical motion are unchanged.
# - Existing LONG_PULL diagnostics from vla_0848 are preserved unchanged.
# vla_0848 diagnostic-only LONG_PULL plan observability patch.
# - Adds AUTO-X log diagnostics for existing ACTION3/LONG_PULL preview + motion-plan resolution.
# - Reuses already-computed heatmap/planner values only: no extra snapshot, YOLO, Pose, heatmap, CCA, or candidate search.
# - Logs A144 strong/fallback/structural candidate counts, selected preview metrics, existing rejection notes, and build_targeted_press_motion_plan.last_diagnostics.
# - LONG_PULL thresholds, candidate ordering, robot geometry, workspace/path safety, motion, and training eligibility are unchanged.
# vla_0847: POST_FINISH ARM2-first robust close + post-close stability + fast final clear.
# - RoArm-M2-S T:104 `t` is the EoAT/end-joint (gripper) angle, not an independent wrist/tool orientation. Preserve OPEN t while approaching/descending and CLOSED t while lifting/carrying; T:106 remains the explicit gripper command path.
# - Move the redundant OPEN re-confirm from the cloth-contact GRIP point to the already-safe high-Z XY-aligned hover stage. After GRIP-DOWN stability passes, no OPEN command is allowed before CLOSE.
# - CLOSE is now fail-closed and sequential: ARM2 CLOSE is sent first and repeated (2x default), then ARM1 CLOSE is sent once. After settle, BOTH arms must pass the GRIP contact/stability barrier again before any LIFT command.
# - Final post-release VERTICAL-CLEAR keeps its existing arrival safety check but uses a dedicated short timeout (2.5s default) instead of the generic 8s POST_FINISH timeout, eliminating the long high-Z dwell before standby.
# - Dedicated POST_FINISH trace distinguishes T:104 eoat_t_rad from T:106 gripper commands and records ARM2 close repeats/order, post-close barrier, and clear-timeout override. Safe-pair geometry, contact Z windows, carry/place paths, and FINISH-save ordering are unchanged.
# vla_0846: POST_FINISH staged safe-hover -> XY-align -> synchronized Z descent + stable PLACE contact barrier.
# - POST_FINISH no longer sends a diagonal XYZ approach directly toward the grasp point. Both arms first rise vertically at their measured current XY to each arm's resolved approach/safe-hover Z and must pass a feedback arrival barrier.
# - Only after BOTH arms are confirmed high do they move horizontally at that high Z to the frozen grasp XY. A second dual-arm XY+Z arrival barrier must pass before any downward command is allowed.
# - GRIP-DOWN remains fail-closed and stability-aware, but the observed near-target allowance is 25mm above target (10mm below) so a physically settled wrist is not rejected by a sub-millimetre threshold edge.
# - PLACE-HOLD now uses the same bounded-depth + measured-Z-stability logic as GRIP-DOWN instead of the old strict +/-10mm target-error barrier. Too-high, still-moving, XY-misaligned, or overshot wrists remain blocked.
# - Existing safe-pair planner, lift/carry/clear barriers, POST_FINISH dedicated trace, recovery, private-workspace/path safety, and FINISH-save-before-postprocess ordering are preserved.
# vla_0845: POST_FINISH mask-interior adaptive safe-pair fallback.
# - Preserve the existing Pose semantic pair and multi-fraction leading-edge mask planners as the primary path. Only when both fail, search the real garment-mask interior separately inside ARM2/ARM1 private workspaces.
# - Interior candidates are spatially grid-sampled, must remain inside the real mask with the existing minimum mask-depth requirement, board/private workspace, affine and RoArm XYZ safety, and must have at least one safe synchronized translation >= the configured minimum move.
# - Remove the POST_FINISH 135mm hard pair-distance rejection. 160mm remains only a preferred tier; adaptive width ratio versus the currently available safe garment width lets small garments use narrower physically-safe pairs.
# - Pair selection is fail-closed on safety, then ranks full requested translation, similar leading depth, preferred/wide adaptive span, two-sided mask depth, workspace margin, and proximity to the ID0-ID2 leading side.
# - POST_FINISH plan/trace diagnostics now record primary planner failure, interior candidate/pair counts, rejection reasons, selected pair width/depth/workspace/path metrics, and adaptive-width rationale. No GRIP/LIFT/CARRY motion timing or barrier parameters are changed in this version.
# vla_0844: POST_FINISH grip-ready barrier uses sufficient descent + measured Z stability before CLOSE.
# - GRIP-DOWN no longer requires both wrists to reach commanded Z within a fixed +/-10mm window. A wrist may stop slightly above the commanded cloth Z, but only inside a bounded near-target window and only after its measured Z has stabilized.
# - Default grip-ready window: XY <= 25mm, no more than 22mm above target Z, no more than 10mm below target Z; both arms must also have <=2mm Z change for 3 consecutive feedback intervals before CLOSE.
# - OPEN re-confirm -> CLOSE -> settle -> LIFT remains strictly after the new dual-arm grip-ready barrier; moving/too-high/too-low arms fail closed into the existing recovery path.
# - POST_FINISH TXT/JSONL now records z_offset_from_target, per-sample Z delta, depth-window result, stability result, and the exact grip-ready pass/timeout reason.
# - No changes to POST_FINISH geometry/speed/carry/lift/place targets, SPREAD exact binding, AUTO-X timeout/grace, mask fallback, ACTION3, ORTHO, or ROTATE behavior in this version.
# vla_0843: dedicated POST_FINISH execution trace + reachability/barrier diagnostics.
# - POST_FINISH now writes its own append-only TXT + JSONL trace AFTER the AUTO-X cycle log has already closed, so GRIP/CLOSE/LIFT/every CARRY waypoint/PLACE/release/recovery/standby are not lost.
# - Every POST_FINISH motion command records the exact ARM2/ARM1 robot XYZ target; every arrival-barrier sample records target XYZ, actual feedback XYZ, XY/Z error, tolerance decision, consecutive-stability count, PASS/TIMEOUT, and elapsed time.
# - Before sending motion, a diagnostic reachability audit records configured RoArm XYZ safety for approach/grip/lift/place/clear and every synchronized carry waypoint, plus board/private-workspace checks where board coordinates are available. Existing planner safety remains authoritative; this audit does not relax any gate.
# - POST_FINISH trace files are stored under the same VLA episode in post_finish_logs/, preserving terminal VLA labels while making the separate post-process fully debuggable. Logging failures are non-fatal and never change robot motion.
# - No changes to SPREAD exact binding, POST_FINISH motion geometry/barrier tolerances, AUTO-X timeout/grace, mask fallback, ACTION3, ORTHO, or ROTATE behavior in this version.
# vla_0842: fallback-color pose validation + empty-baseline diagnostics + ACTION3 safe-clear fallback.
# - fallback_color no longer hard-rejects solely at 45% board coverage: <=45% keeps the normal path, 45..58% is marked PENDING_POSE and is accepted only when a fresh same-snapshot Pose has sufficient keypoint support inside/near that exact color mask; >58% remains MASK_SUSPECT.
# - Existing fallback_color trusted-area growth veto remains a hard safety veto and is not relaxed. A conditional color mask is never published to the planner before Pose validation completes.
# - When bgdiff is implausibly quiet while a substantial color object exists, emit EMPTY_BASELINE_SUSPECT with bgdiff mean/foreground ratio. This is diagnostic-only and does not by itself block an otherwise validated mask.
# - ACTION3 strict return-clear target/tolerance remains unchanged. If one arm stalls short of the -5mm return target but is already stably at/above its previously validated legacy vertical-clear height, classify SAFE_CLEAR_FALLBACK and OPEN -> full standby immediately instead of waiting for a misleading strict-clear timeout.
# - ACTION3 clear verification now also audits XY error; unsafe/low clear states still fail closed into the existing OPEN + full-standby recovery.
# - No changes to SPREAD exact binding, POST_FINISH arrival barriers, ORTHO, ROTATE, or AUTO-X fresh timeout/grace behavior in this version.
# vla_0841: AUTO-X fresh-observation timeout/grace synchronization.
# - AUTO-X fresh observation now treats auto_align_rotate_fresh_timeout as a SOFT timeout (15s default), not immediate NO_ACTION_CANDIDATE.
# - If AUTO-X snapshot capture/burst or YOLO/pose/planner inference is still in flight at the soft deadline, wait an additional inflight grace window (10s default).
# - If inference is still actively running after grace, keep waiting for that SAME logical snapshot up to a bounded hard fail-safe (45s total default); do not launch a competing rejudge while the worker is active.
# - A hard capture/inference wait failure is classified as AUTO_X_FRESH_WAIT_TECHNICAL_TIMEOUT, cancels/discards the stale request/result, and does NOT increment/schedule NO_ACTION_CANDIDATE rejudge.
# - A genuinely completed fresh inference with no usable candidate/plan still follows the existing bounded NO_ACTION_CANDIDATE rejudge policy unchanged.
# - No changes to SPREAD exact binding, POST_FINISH arrival barriers, ORTHO, ROTATE, mask fallback, or ACTION3 behavior in this version.
# vla_0840: POST_FINISH actual-arrival grip barrier and fail-closed stage synchronization.
# - POST_FINISH no longer treats a fixed descend sleep as proof that both arms reached the cloth. After vertical-down, ARM2 and ARM1 must both report the frozen grip XYZ for consecutive feedback samples before any CLOSE command is allowed.
# - Grip arrival uses a dedicated tighter Z tolerance (10mm default); an OPEN command is reasserted only after both arms are confirmed at grip height, then CLOSE -> dedicated settle -> LIFT.
# - LIFT and PLACE also receive POST_FINISH arrival barriers so one arm cannot begin carry/release while the other arm is still vertically catching up. Existing synchronized carry waypoint barriers remain unchanged.
# - Any POST_FINISH arrival timeout fails closed: no lift/carry is started from an unconfirmed grip, and recovery opens the grippers then prefers each arm's ACTUAL feedback XY for a vertical high-clear before standby.
# - No changes to SPREAD exact binding, ORTHO, ROTATE, timeout/rejudge, mask fallback, or ACTION3 behavior in this version.
# vla_0839: SPREAD exact-plan binding from X judgment to preview and execution.
# - Every VLA X judgment now builds/finalizes one same-snapshot Step37+A91 NORMAL SPREAD plan before publishing the pending decision, even when AUTO-X selected another macro.
# - The frozen Step37+A91 plan is stored in pending and is the only plan a later human SPREAD selection may bind; the human override path is forbidden from rebuilding SPREAD geometry.
# - While WAITING_ENTER, the on-screen SPREAD debug overlay uses this exact frozen plan and draws the actual A91 forced physical pull direction, not the earlier coarse/base spread axis.
# - A deterministic binding id is stored and rechecked before execution so preview/selection/execution geometry cannot silently diverge.
# - No changes to ORTHO, POST_FINISH, ROTATE, timeout/rejudge, mask fallback, or ACTION3 behavior in this version.
# vla_0838: ORTHO_SPREAD post-stretch release/return is bound to the proven Step37 SEGMENTATION_SPREAD cleanup path.
# - ACTION5 ORTHO keeps its vla_0832 midpoint-normal ray-fan contacts, dynamic pull, and exact orthogonal stretch axis unchanged.
# - After the orthogonal stretch reaches its lifted endpoint, ORTHO now uses the SAME cleanup policy as Step37 ACTION2: air OPEN at stretch-lift -> same-XY vertical retract -> imaging standby.
# - The old ORTHO floor-place / slow-open cleanup override is disabled only for ACTION5; gray ambiguity probe and other actions keep their existing behavior.
# - This removes low-Z post-release cloth contact that could rotate/re-wrinkle the garment during ORTHO return.
# vla_0837: POST_FINISH pose-freeze + soft pair fallback + synchronized lifted translation/release smoothing.
# - Freeze one POST_FINISH_TOP_ALIGN plan from the same snapshot when FINISH is selected; Enter first records/terminates the VLA episode, then executes this separate post-process only if the frozen plan is safe.
# - Prefer pose-semantic anchors: whichever of neck/shoulder side vs waist/hem side is closer to the ID0-ID2 edge; use shoulder_left/right or waist_left/right, inset ~35mm toward garment centroid, and require >=25mm real-mask interior depth.
# - If pose anchors are unavailable/unsafe, search several garment-mask leading-edge lateral pairs (20/80, 25/75, 30/70, 35/65), then apply centroid-directed inset and mask-depth validation.
# - Use two-arm low-lift rigid translation: OPEN -> high approach -> vertical grip -> CLOSE once -> low lift -> identical board-space vector toward ID0-ID2 -> place down -> OPEN -> same-XY clear -> standby.
# - Desired distance is computed from garment leading-edge distance to ID0-ID2 minus a target ~25mm margin. The old CENTER 150mm cap is NOT used; board/private-workspace/affine/XYZ/path safety may back off or skip the optional post-process.
# - POST_FINISH_TOP_ALIGN never opens a VLA transition and does not call the AUTO-X action execution/result accounting path.
# vla_0834: ROTATE_PULL soft long-lever / wide-pair preference.
# - Do NOT add a new hard minimum pair-distance gate; the existing 160mm initial safety gate remains unchanged.
# - Cap candidate rotation-effect reward at the requested target (effect_ratio <= 1.0), so over-rotation estimates receive no extra ranking bonus.
# - Among target-reaching safe candidates, softly prefer candidates retaining >=55% of their ideal centroid-ray leverage/pair span, then prefer larger lever and wider grip-pair span.
# - If no target-reaching long-lever candidate exists, shorter safe candidates remain available as fallback; path/workspace/pair-stretch safety is unchanged.
# vla_0832: replace ACTION5 ORTHO planner with regular-SPREAD midpoint normal-ray fan geometry.
# - Start from the FINAL regular SPREAD grip pair, use its midpoint, and cast a fan of rays around the exact perpendicular axis (0, +/-5, +/-10, +/-15, +/-20deg by default).
# - Intersect each ray with the real garment-mask boundary on both sides, inset both contacts toward the midpoint (25mm default), then validate real-mask inclusion, private ARM2/ARM1 workspaces, board bounds, pair distance, and final 90+/-20deg orthogonality.
# - Remove the old ORTHO endpoint projection-band search and its board-y difference <=180mm gate; true near-vertical ORTHO geometry is no longer rejected merely for having large y separation.
# - Rank only safe ray candidates, preferring larger usable pair/span, better workspace/mask support, and smaller deviation from exact 90deg. Existing same-snapshot ORTHO pre-freeze and execution safety/backoff are preserved.
# vla_0831: SPREAD final-axis binding + ORTHO same-snapshot prefreeze/diagnostics.
# - Apply A91 minor/short-axis forcing to the FINAL Step37 ACTION2 execution plan, including human SPREAD override.
#   This prevents board_x/board_y fallback contacts from changing the physical pull direction after the on-screen decision.
# - In VLA mode, precompute/freeze a safe ORTHO_SPREAD alternative from the current regular SPREAD snapshot BEFORE
#   CENTER/ROTATE/FINISH priority returns, so human ORTHO override does not lose the same-snapshot ACTION5 plan.
# - Preserve ORTHO plan source/status in pending records and report the exact unavailable reason on human override.
# - Existing ACTION5 board/private-workspace/pair-distance/final-orthogonality safety gates are unchanged.
# vla_0830: enable normal training eligibility for newly collected ROTATE transitions.
# - Remove the global ROTATE training quarantine: ROTATE now follows the same eligibility rule as other macros.
# - A ROTATE transition becomes training_eligible=True only when it is GOOD, execution_success=True, garment_motion_committed=True, execution_sent=True, has valid before/after observations, neither mask is MASK_INACCURATE, and there is no execution-action binding mismatch.
# - BAD/SKIP ROTATE remains training-ineligible. Existing recorded transitions are not rewritten.
# - ROTATE_PULL/SHEAR motion, 12deg/18deg hysteresis, grip/path/workspace/pair-stretch safety, and all other action logic are unchanged.
# vla_0829: preserve safe frozen ROTATE preview in FINISH human-confirmation pending state.
# - Fix VLA human ROTATE override reporting ROTATE_PLAN_UNAVAILABLE after FINISH_READY_FOR_ROTATION even when a READY ROTATE_PULL/SHEAR plan is visible and A153-safe.
# - FINISH/HUMAN_FINISH now stores vla_safe_pose_rotation_plan using the same READY and not-DONE rule as ordinary pending actions.
# - ROTATE geometry/strength, 12deg/18deg hysteresis, SHEAR, pair-stretch, workspace/path safety, and training eligibility are unchanged.
# vla_0828: stronger large-angle ROTATE_PULL preference without adding a new hard gate.
# - Keep the vla_0827 12deg/18deg AUTO-X hysteresis and all vla_0826 tension-reduction/safety behavior.
# - For ROTATE_PULL errors above 18deg, gradually raise the requested rotation effect; the boost reaches 1.20x by 30deg and the target cap may rise from 30deg to 34deg.
# - Safe joint-grip candidates are still all considered; at larger errors, candidate ranking gives slightly more weight to actual planned rotation effect while retaining the existing pair-stretch penalty.
# - No candidate is rejected merely for producing less than the boosted target. If a larger safe plan does not exist, the existing smaller safe 40..120mm PULL remains available.
# - PULL backoff now checks 10mm distance steps (plus exact base/minimum), preventing a coarse scale jump from skipping a safe medium-strength plan and falling straight to 40mm.
# - outward_mix=0.10, 45mm pair-stretch hard safety, SHEAR, legacy-ARC disable, fast grip timing, ORTHO gate, unlimited collection actions, and ROTATE training exclusion remain unchanged.
# vla_0827: AUTO-X small-angle ROTATE hysteresis (12deg align / 18deg re-arm).
# - After a confirmed/reliable <=12deg rotation error, latch ROTATE as aligned for the current garment cycle.
# - While latched, ordinary AUTO-X ROTATE is suppressed through 18deg so SPREAD-induced 12..18deg wobble does not cause ROTATE<->SPREAD ping-pong.
# - The latch releases only when a fresh usable angle exceeds 18deg; then the existing PULL/SHEAR planner, confirmation, and all safety checks apply unchanged.
# - Pose planner deadband remains 8deg, ROTATE_PULL trajectory/tension settings remain vla_0826, ROTATE stays training-excluded, and SHEAR/ORTHO/YOLO/action-count policies are unchanged.
# vla_0826: ROTATE_PULL tension reduction + final ORTHO-axis gate + unlimited VLA collection actions.
# - ROTATE_PULL outward radial mix is reduced 0.25 -> 0.10; tangent/rotation component, 40..120mm pull range, and existing 45mm hard pair-stretch safety gate remain.
# - Joint grip-pair search evaluates the bounded safe grip pairs and ranks rotation effect against pair-stretch instead of stopping at the first safe high-grip-quality pair.
# - ROTATE_SHEAR is unchanged. Legacy ARC / pair-distance-locked rotation is not re-enabled. ROTATE remains training-excluded.
# - ORTHO_SPREAD is allowed only when the FINAL selected grip axis stays within 20deg of perpendicular to the current regular SPREAD grip axis.
# - VLA data collection no longer pauses or fails because an action count was reached; --auto-x-max-actions is diagnostic only.
# vla_0824: ROTATE_PULL joint grip-pair search.
# - Keeps the existing 10deg centroid-ray, 20mm midpoint-symmetry, mask inset, pair-distance/stretch, workspace, board and torque safety gates unchanged.
# - Replaces one-sided seed->single opposite projection with a bounded joint search over spatially diverse mask-interior candidates on both arm rays.
# - Chooses a pair only when the final two grips themselves satisfy the original symmetry/opposite-diagonal/torque/path constraints; no tolerance is relaxed.
# - Preserves vla_0823 exact-minimum pull fix, vla_0822 semantic 160mm ROTATE gate, waypoint soft-pass, post-grip recovery, recovery-key split and angle-confirmation fixes.
# vla_0823: ROTATE linear-planner minimum-distance numeric fix + reject diagnostics.
# - Fix ROTATE_PULL minimum 40mm candidate loss caused by rounding min_scale to 6 decimals (e.g. 39.99996mm < 40mm).
# - Apply the same exact-minimum scale handling to ROTATE_SHEAR because it used the identical rounding pattern.
# - Keep all existing geometry/workspace/pair-stretch safety limits unchanged; this patch only prevents valid minimum-distance candidates from false rejection.
# - Add structured linear-plan reject diagnostics (MIN_PULL/PAIR_STRETCH/SYMMETRY/WORKSPACE/BOARD_BOUND/RAY_ERROR/etc.) when geometry cannot be built.
# - ROTATE remains experimental/training_eligible=False; vla_0822 semantic gate, waypoint soft-pass, recovery, key split, and angle-confirmation fixes are preserved.
# vla_0822: ROTATE safety/state fixes after 2026-08-21 board tests.
# - Keep the legacy 80mm pose-axis validity threshold for pose inference/diagnostics, but add a separate 160mm semantic neck-waist gate for physical ROTATE decisions.
# - Airborne ROTATE WAYPOINT arrival keeps the normal 25mm XY tolerance and permits only a stalled 25..30mm near-limit soft-pass with normal Z tolerance.
# - Any failure after ROTATE close-at-grip starts uses one generic FULL-OPEN -> actual-current-XY vertical clear -> confirmed standby recovery; the failed action remains failed.
# - Physical-recovery acknowledgement is moved from A to '.'; A remains garment/AUTO-X reset and no longer clears the safety latch.
# - FINAL angle-confirmation latch is armed on every FINAL confirmation wait, preventing a transient CCA FINAL->MID flip from discarding the one fresh angle sample.
# - VLA provenance is bumped; ROTATE remains experimental/training_eligible=False.
# vla_0815_v13: v12 plus same-garment rejudge hard-stop and persistent one-shot Pose-retry latch; MASK_SHAPE ROTATE remains enabled/experimental.
# - MASK_SHAPE_FALLBACK is intentionally NOT disabled in v13. It may still publish/execute an experimental ROTATE after its existing one-fresh confirmation and normal geometry/workspace/path safety checks.
# - Once the single fresh Pose retry has been consumed for a garment_motion_count, it cannot reopen until a real garment motion changes garment_motion_count. Cache/mask fallback success does not reset that latch.
# - Fallback/Pose acceptance no longer resets the generic internal-rejudge counter. This prevents Pose->mask fallback->Late rejudge from restarting at attempt 1 forever.
# - A separate same-garment automatic-rejudge hard cap (default follows the existing generic max, minimum 2) stops cross-label rejudge loops even when planner labels change. The next state is a single VLA HUMAN DECISION hold, not another automatic snapshot.
# - ROTATE source is logged explicitly as POSE/FULL_FRAME/LAST_VALID/MASK_AXIS/MASK_SHAPE with angle/exact-action readiness for later experimental evaluation.
# - Human macro selection is bound to the CURRENT frozen action, not the original planner macro. Selecting an unavailable macro converts the pending item to a no-motion HUMAN_REJUDGE hold; Enter can never execute the stale previous plan.
# - Enter performs a final human-macro/exact-action binding audit before opening a transition. Any mismatch blocks robot motion and transition creation.
# - VLA transition executed_action is always the exact pending dispatcher action actually sent to the executor; stale vla_executed_action_override metadata can no longer relabel another motion.
# - Pose recovery is exactly current failure + ONE fresh retry. After that, same-motion cache -> mask-axis/mask-shape fallback is attempted without allowing failure counters to grow beyond the configured budget.
# - If Pose/cache/mask rotation recovery is exhausted, only ROTATE is unavailable for that observation. CENTER/SPREAD/LONG_PULL and the ordinary planner remain available; the old ROTATE hard-hold/Human-Hold loop is removed.
# - TOP mask-shape fallback supplements PCA ratio gating: when the silhouette is nearly square, body-axis selection may use end-width/profile asymmetry across the two PCA axis families. It remains a low-trust source and receives exactly one fresh confirmation.
# - Rotation rejudge labels are separated into ROTATE_POSE_RETRY_REQUIRED, ROTATE_FALLBACK_CONFIRM_REJUDGE, and ROTATE_ANGLE_CONFIRM_REJUDGE. The legacy ROTATE_POSE_CONSENSUS_REJUDGE is retained only for historical compatibility and is no longer generated.
# - ROTATE deadband remains 8deg. Reliable ROI/full-frame Pose above the 8..14deg boundary-confirm band publishes ROTATE immediately.
# - Pose recovery remains current failure + one additional fresh failure (2 total) -> same-motion cache -> mask-axis fallback.
# - A successful LAST_VALID_POSE_CACHE/MASK_AXIS_FALLBACK opens a separate one-confirmation rejudge budget, so the preceding Pose retry no longer consumes the confirmation allowance and prematurely causes VLA HUMAN DECISION REQUIRED.
# - If low-trust confirmation is already pending, the next same-motion Pose failure rebuilds cache/mask-axis immediately; it does not restart the Pose retry sequence or reset the confirmation budget again.
# - 8..14deg near-boundary angles and low-trust sources still require exactly one fresh angle confirmation; clear reliable Pose angles do not.
# - Ambiguous/Pose-recovery CIRCUMCENTER_NUDGE now hard-caps both Circumcenter-specific base/final pull limits to the advertised nudge max, so a 15..45mm nudge cannot become a 100mm+ pull.
# - Invalid/missing linear ROTATE targets remain distinct from true initial grip-pair-distance blocks; added explicit Pose/fallback/confirmation log tags make non-selection causes visible.
# - ROTATE_PULL fixed 30mm behavior is removed: target effect = clamp(|error|*0.80, 10..30deg), distance is derived from actual mask-centroid lever arms and clamped to 40..120mm.
# - ROTATE_PULL planned_effect_deg is recomputed from the final commanded endpoints after clamp/path-safety scaling.
# - ROTATE_SHEAR keeps gain 0.55 / target 22..35deg / 60..160mm, but its absolute pair-stretch allowance is 80mm; PULL and all other motions keep the existing 45mm limit.
# - Legacy ARC planning is no longer used as the precursor for new ROTATE. Pose/Mask now provide only current axis + semantic seed hints; PULL/SHEAR build their own grips and paths.
# - ROTATE_PULL uses the actual garment-mask centroid, ray-preserving point symmetry, hard opposite-diagonal grip validation, torque-correct straight pulls, and no shoulder-pair fallback.
# - ROTATE_SHEAR is independent of shoulder keypoints and uses dynamic same-y 60-160mm planning (gain 0.55, target effect 22-35deg) with fresh rejudge.
# - AUTO-X publishes/executes ROTATE_PULL or ROTATE_SHEAR directly. ROTATE_MID/ROTATE_FINAL remain historical compatibility strings only, never generated as pending physical actions.
# - Legacy MID gates (spread>=3, angle>=30, executable arc delta>=15, one-MID budget/cooldown) and FINAL rotate-count STOP are no longer used. Rotate counters remain diagnostics only.
# - Pose recovery is current failure + one additional fresh failure -> same-motion cached Pose -> mask-axis/mask-shape fallback; if all fail, ROTATE soft-blocks while ordinary planner remains available. Physical motion clears cached Pose/retry latches.
# - Trusted FALLBACK_BGDIFF remains allowed for both PULL/SHEAR; all experimental ROTATE transitions remain training_eligible=False.
# - Trusted FALLBACK_BGDIFF planning masks may drive ROTATE_PULL/ROTATE_SHEAR after the normal board-clip, area/shape, and Lab-veto sanitation passes. FALLBACK_COLOR remains blocked.
# - ROTATE_SHEAR no longer uses a fixed 35mm pull: per-arm distance is derived from same-y grip span and a bounded 22-35deg target effect, clamped to 60-160mm, then planned_effect_deg is recomputed from the final commanded distance.
# - Legacy circular/arc ROTATE planning/execution is disabled. ROTATE_MID/ROTATE_FINAL survive only as historical-import compatibility strings, never as current planner/executor actions.
# - During transient pose loss, the garment is held still while fresh Pose observations complete the configured retry sequence; then same-motion cache -> mask-axis fallback is attempted.
# - Every ROTATE macro transition in this experimental release is forced training_eligible=False, regardless of exact variant or GOOD/BAD/SKIP label.
# - ROTATE_PULL no longer uses fixed ARM2 -x / ARM1 +x spreading motion; centroid-ray retarget is capped at 10deg and final midpoint symmetry error is hard-limited.
# - Each grip moves along the required rotation tangent plus a small radial-outward component, creating rotation torque while keeping cloth tension.
# - Left/right shoulder-side Pose points are evaluated only as independent seed hints; the old two-shoulder execution pair is never reused.
# - ROTATE_PULL never scales below the configured minimum pull (40mm default); if >=40mm is unsafe, that candidate is blocked instead of doing a weak pull.
# - ROTATE_NO_IMPROVEMENT and all rotate counters are diagnostic/nonblocking; fresh planning may continue subject only to consensus and physical safety.
# - Experimental ROTATE transitions are recorded normally but every ROTATE macro is forced training_eligible=False until explicitly re-enabled.
# - Post-final repair budget exhaustion no longer STOPs AUTO-X; it ends the repair phase and returns to the ordinary planner.
# - Ambiguous/Pose-recovery CIRCUMCENTER_NUDGE reaches the high-Z XY target (feedback-confirmed) before sending contact Z.
# - Transient ROTATE pose loss gets bounded fresh-observation retries, then same-motion last-valid-pose reuse, then conservative mask-axis fallback.
# rotate_pull_v1 (2026-08-15): replace board-contact arc ROTATE with lift + straight-pull primitives.
# - |angle error| > 45deg: ROTATE_SHEAR uses same-y left/right mask-inset grips and opposite +/-board-y straight pulls.
# - Historical rotate_pull_v1 used 12deg < |angle error| <= 45deg for ROTATE_PULL; v10 overrides the active deadband to 8deg.
#   retargeted into mask-inset + each arm private workspace, then uses torque-directed tangent pulls with a small outward-tension component.
# - New linear ROTATE skips pre-slack, circular 10deg arc waypoints, and the legacy rigid-pair +3mm lock.
#   Existing grip/lift Z, arrival barriers, board/XYZ/workspace safety, release/vertical-retract/standby, and motion_v7 lift recovery remain.
# press_override_fix1 historical note: standalone ACTION4/VLA PRESS is retired in vla_0852_stage1.
# vla_statefix1: motion_v7 plus VLA non-executable-decision recovery and override callback protection.
# - FINAL rotation pose/plan uncertainty requests a bounded fresh rejudge instead of immediately STOPping the VLA cycle.
# - If bounded rejudge attempts are exhausted, keep the current observation in a human-decision hold so VLA macro buttons remain usable.
# - VLA mouse override exceptions restore the previous frozen pending state instead of breaking the control flow.
# vla_statefix2: statefix1 plus ROTATE full-frame pose fallback and explicit MASK ACCURATE review label.
# - ROTATE first keeps the existing ArUco-ROI pose inference. Only perception failures retry the SAME corrected snapshot full-frame.
# - A full-frame fallback pose is accepted only when enough pose keypoints overlap the current garment segmentation mask.
# - MASK ACCURATE is stored separately from GOOD/BAD/SKIP and marks a reviewed segmentation mask as fine-tuning eligible.
# motion_v7: motion_v6 plus ARM2 ROTATE lift reachability fix and automatic LIFT-HOLD failure recovery.
# - ARM2 uses 0mm ROTATE-only extra lift by default (base lift ~= -80mm); ARM1 keeps the existing +20mm extra lift.
# - If ROTATE LIFT-HOLD command/arrival fails after gripping, automatically FULL-OPEN -> same-XY hover retract -> confirmed camera-clear standby.
# - If that recovery completes, no '.' physical-recovery acknowledgement is required; the failed ROTATE still remains execution_success=False.
# motion_v6: motion_v5 plus FINAL-confirmation latch, safe VLA ROTATE override, and 10-degree commanded ROTATE waypoints.
# - Keep pre-slack, but never let the gripper pair shrink below 160mm before rotation.
# motion_v4: motion_v3 plus ROTATE grip-quality/reachability fixes from 2026-08-10 logs.
# - ROTATE-only ARM1 grip Z override (shallower reachable target; default -102mm).
# - Require >=2 pose keypoints per semantic grip side before accepting pose_original.
# - Require >=160mm initial ROTATE grip-pair distance; existing 80mm path safety remains unchanged.
# motion_v3: motion_v2 plus VLA fresh before/after ACTION2 plateau-feedback wiring fix.
# General SPREAD keeps the original A79 3% plateau / -25mm policy; only the stale-evaluation
# connection is fixed. ACTION5 ORTHOGONAL_SPREAD selection conditions remain untouched.
# motion_v2: VLA capture/return reliability + adaptive spread-distance policy/provenance.
# vla_0805.py: step_a150-3-18 plus TOP-garment SmolVLA macro-action dataset collection.
# The A150 motion/planner/safety implementation remains the executor. This patch only records
# observations, planner proposals, human macro corrections, exact executed variants, execution
# success/failure, before/after observations, and GOOD/BAD/SKIP labels. Current exact
# ROTATE_PULL/ROTATE_SHEAR are stored as macro ROTATE; old MID/FINAL names are read only for historical compatibility.
# VLA collection mode disables ACTION3 auto-execution so every physical action requires Enter.
# step_a150-3-17.py: step_a150-3-16 plus private-workspace-first pose-rotation grasp selection.
# The original pose shoulder/sleeve grasp pair remains first priority. A grasp is executable only when
# ARM2 starts in the ID0/ID1 private zone and ARM1 starts in the ID2/ID3 private zone. If a raw pose
# grasp crosses the split, normal semantic YOLO garment mask points are searched toward each arm side
# at 20/40/60mm, then near the garment region closest to the ID0-ID2 line as a last grasp fallback.
# This legacy A157 semantic-grip retarget still excludes fallback masks; the later v5 linear ROTATE converter independently accepts only trusted/sanitized FALLBACK_BGDIFF and performs its own mask/workspace retarget. Soft workspace
# remains available only after the private-zone initial grip, for the lifted rotation path. One alternate
# fully validated private-zone grasp pair may be retried after a grip-arrival timeout; a second failure aborts.
# step_a150-3-16.py: step_a150-3-15 plus A156 rotation/auto-execution refinements.
# Static structural probe keeps the passive arm OPEN at imaging standby and commands only the active arm.
# Historical step_a150-3-16 behavior: a too-small ROTATE_MID plan was re-gripped inward at 20/40/60mm; v6 does not call that legacy helper.
# candidate with the largest executable angle is selected, and sub-threshold MID does not consume its budget.
# Pose rotation uses a dedicated +20mm lift offset and T:105 arrival barriers at grip, lift, pre-slack,
# every commanded 10-degree waypoint, and place. ACTION3 normal/reduced/Late-Strong can auto-execute after
# a short frozen-plan preview; the existing target-invalidation watcher cancels it if the garment moves.
# step_a150-3-13.py: step_a150-3-12 plus A153 pose-rotation soft-workspace validation.
# Only the static ARM2-left/ARM1-right private-workspace rule is softened for pose rotation.
# Every otherwise-ready rotation is promoted only after complete paired-path validation of
# board bounds, affine conversion, RoArm XYZ limits, minimum pair distance, left/right order,
# pre-slack, all stepwise rotation waypoints, place, and vertical retract. All other blocks remain hard.
# step_a150-3-12.py: step_a150-3-11 plus A152 AUTO-X MID/FINAL pose-rotation integration.
# Historical step_a150-3-12 behavior used ROTATE_MID/ROTATE_FINAL pending names; v6 emits exact ROTATE_PULL/ROTATE_SHEAR instead.
# One fresh judgment selects at most one physical action. Rotation uses confidence-aware
# conditional angle confirmation, center-first priority, bounded final repair/rotation budgets,
# post-rotation effectiveness checks, and the existing full Planner after every rotate.
# Automatic rotation always performs exactly one <=40deg physical rotation per action;
# manual key-6 hover-only/auto-loop behavior remains independently configurable.
# step_a150-3-14.py: step_a150-3-13 plus A154 verified ACTION3/Late Strong return-clear at board Z=-5mm.
# ACTION3 never starts the active sweep from a fixed timer alone: T:105 feedback must confirm
# both the active and passive-hold arms reached their own contact targets for consecutive samples.
# Feedback timeout/failure cancels the sweep, vertically clears both arms, then uses the existing
# full-open and standby cleanup path. Soft workspace hold remains enabled.
# Circumcenter-only 120mm base cap, 1.25 scale, 150mm final cap, and -80mm lift defaults are preserved.
# Only ordinary CENTER_CIRCUMCENTER (including key-1 override) changes from low-Z Press-Drag
# to OPEN high approach -> vertical grip-down -> one CLOSE -> vertical Lift -> original XY path
# -> end OPEN -> same-XY vertical clear. Manual '/', Late Circumcenter, and Nudge paths stay Press-Drag.
# Circumcenter/fallback base distance is capped at 120mm, scaled by 1.25, then finally capped at 150mm.
# step_a150-3.py: A150 baseline with manual-X-only AUTO-X cycle start.
# Startup, READY termination, and manual A reset remain idle until the operator presses X.
# After the first 10 physical garment motions, unresolved non-ignored wrinkle regions
# are tracked through up to three valid Late action evaluations.  Only a clearly
# unfinished garment may enter one partial-reset Strong Recovery epoch (max 5 motions)
# before a second Late visit; near-flat garments never return to strong spreading.
# B58 pre-Late probe gate, and B59 profile-aware READY/Late integration are preserved.
# The A136 terminal probe guards, short/slow center-safe probes, and original ACTION1
# circumcenter geometry in Late mode without the A133 distance clip are preserved.
# persistent pose-relative late target tracks, one-main/two-probe A150 limits, and fallback
# direction/arm planning that prevents the same physical wrinkle from being acted on repeatedly.
# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""
Step_a109 integration:
- AUTO-X ACTION2 decision/gating remains unchanged.
- After ACTION2 is selected, grasp planning and dual-arm spread execution use the tuned Step37 minor-first inward-grasp path.
- The exact X snapshot is preserved in pending state; Enter executes without re-inference.

step_a108.py

Dual RoArm + big-table ArUco + YOLO workspace step6 refined grasp-candidate test script.

Step_b2 update:
  - pose rotation correction target angle default changed from -90 deg to +90 deg,
    matching the current live board/homography observation.
  - rotation grip assignment is documented and kept board-x based: smaller x -> ARM2, larger x -> ARM1.
  - POSE ROT overlay now prints A2x/A1x to verify arm assignment.

This version avoids maximum gripper close to reduce servo heating with a 3D-printed extension.

Coordinate layout already applied from user measurement:
  ID0 = (0, 0)
  ID1 = (0, -496)
  ID2 = (492, 5)
  ID3 = (494, -490)
  RED_EXTRA  = (115, -249)  -> ARM2, ID0/ID1 side
  BLUE_EXTRA = (370, -249)  -> ARM1, ID2/ID3 side

Robot placement:
  ARM1: between ID2 and ID3 side. Default port /dev/roarm_1.
  ARM1 and ARM2 are both connected. Step1 workspace split is applied: ARM2 left, ARM1 right, center dead-zone blocked.

Main flow:
  1) Open webcam and detect ArUco ID0, ID1, ID2, ID3.
  2) Press L to lock Homography pixel -> board.
  3) Press C to run ARM1-only affine calibration:
       ARM1: ID2 -> ID3 -> BLUE_EXTRA
  4) Move ARM1 to standby position outside the clothing area after calibration.
  5) In snapshot-grasp mode, wait until the camera view is still,
     freeze one image, and run YOLO on that frozen image.
  6) Press P or Enter to pick the selected candidate with the automatically assigned arm.
  7) By default, lift the cloth a small amount, place it back at the same XY, open, retract, and re-infer.
  8) The gripper is opened immediately at startup and uses limited-close angles by default.

Keys:
A150-3-1 temporary test: key 1 immediately executes one CENTER_CIRCUMCENTER from the latest valid plan.
  L      : lock/save Homography
  R      : reset Homography
  C      : start ARM1-only affine calibration
  Enter  : during calibration, capture current RoArm T:105 coordinate;
           normal mode, run pick at selected grasp point
  P      : run pick at selected grasp point
  1      : select upper_left candidate
  2      : select upper_right candidate
  0      : select center candidate
  F      : feedback ARM1
  G      : open ARM1 gripper
  A      : reset auto-pick state
  Q/ESC  : quit

Recommended normal run (all standard arguments are stored in USER_SETTINGS):
  python3 step_a149.py

Optional CLI arguments can still override USER_SETTINGS for one-off tests.
Example dry run:
  python3 step_a148.py --no-send --dry-run
"""

